---
// Privacy policy text (en). Shared by the live page (pages/en/privacy-policy.astro) and the redesign lab, so the
// legal wording exists once. `demoHref` lets the lab point „Book a demo” at its own demo page.
// Structure: general (1–3) · 4 Website · 5 Application · shared provisions (6–12). Website and app each list
// their own data, purposes, providers and cookies (providers: data/legal.ts, by scope).
import { DEMO_PATH, LEGAL } from '../../consts';
import { appRecipients, webRecipients } from '../../data/legal';
import { getLocale, localizePath } from '../../i18n/utils';

interface Props {
  demoHref?: string;
}
const locale = getLocale(Astro.url);
const { demoHref = localizePath(DEMO_PATH, locale) } = Astro.props;
---

<h2 id="introduction">1. Introduction</h2>
<p>
  {LEGAL.companyName} (“Cargo Navis”, “we”) respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your
  personal data. This policy explains what data we collect, why we process it, who we share it with,
  and what rights you have, separately for:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>the website</strong> <a href="https://www.cargo-navis.com">www.cargo-navis.com</a> (section 4),
    and
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>the Cargo Navis application</strong> <a href="https://app.cargo-navis.com">app.cargo-navis.com</a>,
    including the driver app (section 5).
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  Sections 6 onwards apply to both. We process data in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (the
  General Data Protection Regulation, “GDPR”) and the Croatian Act on the Implementation of the GDPR.
</p>

<h2 id="data-controller">2. Data controller</h2>
<p>The controller of your personal data is:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>{LEGAL.companyName}</strong></li>
  <li>OIB (tax ID): {LEGAL.oib}</li>
  <li>{LEGAL.addressLines.join(', ')}</li>
  <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.privacyEmail}`}>{LEGAL.privacyEmail}</a></li>
</ul>
<p>
  For data our clients enter into the application, Cargo Navis has a different role, as described in
  section 5.1.
</p>

<h2 id="definitions">3. Definitions</h2>
<p>
  <strong>Personal data</strong> means any information relating to an identified or identifiable
  individual - for example a name, email address, phone number or IP address.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Processing</strong> means any operation performed on personal data, including collection,
  recording, storage, use, disclosure and erasure.
</p>

<h2 id="website">4. The website www.cargo-navis.com</h2>

<h3>4.1. Visiting the site</h3>
<p>
  When you visit the site, our server automatically logs the technical data needed to deliver
  content and keep it secure: IP address, browser type and version, operating system, date and time
  of the request, and the requested URL. We do not use tracking cookies or visitor analytics tools.
</p>

<h3>4.2. Booking a demo</h3>
<p>
  If you book a demo through our site, the booking is handled by Google Calendar Appointment
  Schedules. When booking you enter your name, email address and, optionally, a short note about your
  business. We use this data only to organise and hold the meeting and to follow up on your enquiry.
</p>

<h3>4.3. Contacting us by email</h3>
<p>
  When you email us, we process your email address, the content of your message and any other data
  you choose to send, in order to reply to your enquiry.
</p>

<h3>4.4. Purposes and legal bases</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Delivering and securing the website</strong> - legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in
    keeping the site working and protected from abuse.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Booking demos and answering enquiries</strong> - steps taken at your request prior to
    entering into a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)), or our legitimate interest in business communication.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Loading external content (Google Calendar)</strong> - legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)
    GDPR) in showing the demo booking calendar on the site.
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>4.5. Service providers for the website</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Provider</th>
      <th>Processing location</th>
      <th>Purpose</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {
      webRecipients.map((p) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{p.name}</td>
          <td>{p.location.en}</td>
          <td>{p.purpose.en}</td>
        </tr>
      ))
    }
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>4.6. Cookies and external content</h3>
<p>The website uses no analytics, advertising or tracking cookies, and sets no cookies of its own.</p>
<p>
  The <a href={demoHref}>Book a demo</a> page embeds Google Calendar. Opening that page loads the
  content directly from Google's servers, and Google may set its own cookies and process your IP
  address in accordance with{' '}
  <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
    Google's privacy policy
  </a>. If you would rather it did not, you can book by emailing us instead of opening that page.
</p>

<h2 id="application">5. The Cargo Navis application (app.cargo-navis.com)</h2>

<h3>5.1. Who the controller is</h3>
<p>
  For data our clients enter into the application - such as shipments, vehicles, drivers and
  documents - the client is the controller and Cargo Navis acts as a processor, working on the
  client's instructions under a data processing agreement. For user account and application usage
  data, Cargo Navis is the controller.
</p>

<h3>5.2. Data we process</h3>
<p>
  For application users we process account data (name, business email address, role), usage data,
  and the content users enter. For drivers we also process their phone number, so we can send them
  their loadings and unloadings.
</p>

<h3>5.3. Usage analytics</h3>
<p>
  To understand how the application is used and to improve it, we record application usage: pages
  viewed, clicks and actions such as creating a shipment or assigning a vehicle, linked to the user
  account (name, email address, role) and the company. We do not record the text or content users
  enter or see on screen (such as client names, addresses and notes), and we do not record sessions.
  We use PostHog for this, with its data hosted in the European Union.
</p>

<h3>5.4. Purposes and legal bases</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Providing the application</strong> - performance of a contract with the client (Art.
    6(1)(b)) and compliance with legal obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)) for accounting records.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Application usage analytics (PostHog)</strong> - legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR)
    in understanding how the application is used, improving it and fixing errors.
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>5.5. Service providers for the application</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Provider</th>
      <th>Processing location</th>
      <th>Purpose</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {
      appRecipients.map((p) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{p.name}</td>
          <td>{p.location.en}</td>
          <td>{p.purpose.en}</td>
        </tr>
      ))
    }
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>5.6. Cookies and local storage</h3>
<p>
  The application uses cookies and browser local storage that are needed to sign in and to work, for
  example to keep you signed in and to remember your filters and display settings.
</p>
<p>
  The usage analytics tool (PostHog, section 5.3) does not store cookies or any other data in your
  browser: it links actions in the application to your user account once you are signed in.
</p>

<h2 id="recipients">6. Other recipients and transfers outside the EEA</h2>
<p>
  We do not sell personal data. We share it only with the service providers listed in sections 4.5
  and 5.5, to the extent necessary to provide our service. We may also disclose data to competent
  authorities where required by law, and to our accounting and legal advisers, who are bound by
  confidentiality.
</p>
<p>
  The application database is hosted in Germany (Hetzner). Some providers - Vercel, Resend, Google and
  Meta (WhatsApp) - may process data outside the European Economic Area, primarily in the United
  States. Where they do, the transfer relies on the European Commission's Standard Contractual
  Clauses or another valid mechanism under Chapter V of the GDPR.
</p>

<h2 id="retention">7. Retention</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Technical server logs - up to 30 days.</li>
  <li>
    Enquiry and demo correspondence - up to 24 months from the last contact, unless it leads to a
    contract.
  </li>
  <li>Account data - for the duration of the contract and 30 days after it ends.</li>
  <li>Accounting records - 11 years, as required by Croatian accounting and tax law.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="your-rights">8. Your rights</h2>
<p>In relation to your personal data you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Access</strong> - confirmation of whether we process your data, and a copy of it.</li>
  <li><strong>Rectification</strong> - correction of inaccurate or completion of incomplete data.</li>
  <li><strong>Erasure</strong> - deletion of data once it is no longer needed for these purposes.</li>
  <li><strong>Restriction of processing</strong> - in the cases set out in the GDPR.</li>
  <li><strong>Portability</strong> - receipt of your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
  <li><strong>Objection</strong> - to processing based on our legitimate interest.</li>
  <li>
    <strong>Withdrawal of consent</strong> - at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of
    processing before withdrawal.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  Send requests to <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.privacyEmail}`}>{LEGAL.privacyEmail}</a>. We respond
  without undue delay and in any event within one month of receiving the request. Where requests are
  complex or numerous, that period may be extended by a further two months; we will tell you if that
  happens. For data entered into the application by your employer or another of our clients, you can
  also send your request to them as the controller. If you believe your rights have been infringed,
  you may lodge a complaint with the Croatian Personal Data Protection Agency (AZOP),{' '}
  <a href="https://azop.hr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">azop.hr</a>.
</p>

<h2 id="children">9. Children's privacy</h2>
<p>
  Our services are intended for business users and are not directed at anyone under 16. We do not
  knowingly collect children's data. If we learn that we have, we delete it without delay.
</p>

<h2 id="security">10. Security</h2>
<p>
  We apply appropriate technical and organisational safeguards, including encrypted transport (HTTPS),
  least-privilege access control and regular backups.
</p>

<h2 id="changes">11. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>
  We may update this policy from time to time. The date of the last change is shown at the top of the
  page. We will notify users of significant changes by email or in-app notice.
</p>

<h2 id="contact">12. Contact</h2>
<p>
  For any questions about this policy or how we process your data, contact us at{' '}
  <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.privacyEmail}`}>{LEGAL.privacyEmail}</a>.
</p>
